From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:54:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 104/122] Loop strength reduction of a[X+i], a[i+X] and a[X-i]
 with X loop invariant

OptimizeInductionVariables replaced a[i] by a pointer stepping through the
array only for an index that is the counter itself and an element size that
is not a power of 2 (where the scaled index addressing would need a
multiplication). An index X+i, i+X or X-i with X built of constants and
local variables or value parameters that the loop does not change costs
sign extensions and an addition per access; it now becomes a pointer as
well (stepping backwards for X-i), for any element size, for static arrays
without range checks. fannkuch: perm[k-i] in the flip loop (instructions
-6.1%); tests/test/opt/tivlinear1.pp.
